use===== CUSTOMER SUPPORT CASE =====
Case ID   : CS-20240601-00892
Priority  : P1 — Critical
Opened    : 2024-06-01 09:15:00 UTC
Customer  : Acme Corp (Enterprise Tier)
Product   : MyApp v3.2.1
Reporter  : John Smith <john.smith@acmecorp.com>

===== SUBJECT =====
Production down — users unable to login since 09:00 UTC

===== CUSTOMER DESCRIPTION =====
Since approximately 9:00 AM UTC our entire user base is unable to log into the application.
The login page loads fine but after entering credentials the spinner just runs forever and
then shows a generic "Something went wrong" error. This is affecting 100% of our users (~5000 active).
We are in a critical business window (end of quarter processing) and this is causing significant
revenue impact. We need this resolved immediately.

Browser console shows: "Failed to fetch" on POST /api/auth/login
Network tab shows: POST /api/auth/login → Status: (pending) → eventually CORS error

===== ENVIRONMENT =====
Deployment: AWS us-east-1
App Version: 3.2.1 (deployed yesterday at 23:45 UTC)
Database: RDS PostgreSQL 15
Cache: ElastiCache Redis 7.0
Load Balancer: ALB

===== STEPS TO REPRODUCE =====
1. Open https://app.acmecorp.com
2. Enter any valid username and password
3. Click Login
4. Observe: spinner runs indefinitely, then CORS error appears

